5. Where the corresponding source is
------------------------------------
For the engine served to browsers (soffice.wasm, soffice.js, soffice.data and the
files next to them) the complete corresponding source is:

  a. This repository: the patches, the build recipe (build/wasm.sh) and the bridge
     scripts. evidence/artifacts/MANIFEST.sha256 records the sha256 of every engine
     file of each build, so a served file can be matched to the commit that built it.
  b. LibreOffice core at the pinned commit above, from the upstream URLs above.
  c. Qt: our own copy of the two pinned Qt commits, as release assets on this
     repository, so the source stays available even if the upstream fork changes:
       https://github.com/beebeeb-io/office/releases/tag/qt-source-5.15.2-wasm-3d440b7
       qt5-3d440b7787f9b5ba15e5f8bcd7aef39b388f94fa.tar.gz
         sha256 6e41516c14b75cf2b054b6d178a6c9b8ccba004973ed84c05ffb9819e7dae0a1
       qtbase-a320678c85ec8029d5394bcd673d4c208af1de3a.tar.gz
         sha256 60afec12adf59fb542ba0a0e8d8699a7eab9759348c186b6a69a34d4d17d83e8
     build/mirror-qt-source.sh regenerates both tarballs byte for byte.
  d. Emscripten 4.0.10 from the emsdk URL above.

To relink the engine against a modified Qt (LGPL-3.0 section 4(d)(0)): build and
install your Qt, set QT5_INSTALL_DIR to that install, and run build/wasm.sh's GUI steps
(clone-gui, configure-gui, build-gui). The recipe reproduces the combined work.

The notices that ship inside the served engine bundle are bridge/THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.txt,
generated from notices/ and build/tarballs/OFL.txt by build/make-third-party-notices.sh.
